Context

List of improvements and thoughts for axis options refactoring

Make it easier to change one option in one axis 

Currently axes defaults are only used if nothing is supplied to the axes array. 

Problem

When setting any property, all the defaults (type, position etc.) of all the axes are lost. This means that all of the options need to be specified every time.

We want to make it easier to change only one property on one of the chart axes but leave the others as default.

All unspecified axes and properties should still render with defaults.

Suggestions

We now have defaulting of axis based on data.

Perhaps this could be extended to ‘fill in the gaps’ of the user defined options?

Ability to identify and reference an axis

Currently axis objects are provided in an array, and are identified (somewhat) by their position. 

Problem

There is no easy way to refer to a specific axis - e.g. by zoom or annotations modules or for syncing axes.

Axes are linked to series via series keys in the axis options. It is preferable to do this by a reference to the axis within the series options.

Suggestions

Axis should have an ‘id’ - user or auto-generated. 

This should be used in an ‘axis’ property on each series for linking them.

This could be used in other modules and options to reference the axis.

We could fix up the auto-generated one to keep existing behaviour.


Other libraries have ‘xAxis’ and ‘yAxis’ arrays. Is this a better approach?

Too opinionated, does not help with top/bottom, does not work with polar, and gets into the xy problem for horizontal bar.

Theme options for axes have ‘right/left/top/bottom', and integrated UI has ‘horizontal/vertical’.

Polar Axis types

There are 4 polar axis types, angle-category, angle-number, radial-category, radial-number. These have no position. The options for polar axes are similar but not identical to cartesian axes.

Suggestions

Allow angle and radial to be axis positions, with number and category being types.

The type+position tuple would uniquely identify which axis and options to use.

Instead of having angle-category type, there would be type: 'category', position: 'angle'.

Allow angleAxis.shape to automatically affect the unspecified radarAxis.shape.

Remove traces of ‘x' and 'y' in polar axes - these currently appear in error messages.

